        "description": "Return the index of each value among strictly increasing cut points. Inputs are finite one-dimensional float32 or float64 arrays. Values must be nonempty; an empty cut vector assigns index zero to every value. 'upper' places equality above a cut; 'lower' places equality below it. Use NumPy searchsorted without rounding, clipping or casting either input. Return a fresh integer vector with indices from zero through the number of cuts. Inputs remain unchanged. Boundaries, units, class names and interpretation are caller policy; no calibration or learning occurs.",
